From 041c6cdc755274ebb6056b13e2987aa3a060f3a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 28/37] Relay: one transmitter at a time - the Tab5 is kept off
 while a TCI program is connected

The Mac's TCI bridge announces tx=1 in its I/Q listener HELLO, and connects
only while a TCI program (WS, WSJT-X, JTDX) is using it. While it is
connected the relay drops the Tab5's transmit commands (TX;, TA<f>; with
f >= 10 Hz) and answers its relay-timed bursts with TX_DONE status 2, so the
Tab5 can't key the QMX; key-up (TA0;, RX;) always passes. The other way
round, while the Tab5 is keyed, TX; and tones on port 3 (PC software, the TCI
bridge) are dropped. Each refusal is logged as BLOCKED (CAT log and
qmx-relay.log, the latter at most every 10 s). A flag file tab5-tx-always in
the relay folder lets the Tab5 transmit anyway.

Bench test with the fake radio: with no TCI program the Tab5's burst played
(TX_DONE 0); with the TCI test client connected the Tab5's TX;, TA1500.00;
and burst were BLOCKED and the TCI client transmitted; with the Tab5 keyed,
a port-3 TX; and tone were BLOCKED and passed again after the Tab5's RX;.

