index 0a720b01..b9d814af 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ Here’s what the QMX+ PanadapterShared adds on top of upstream QMX-Panadapter,
 * No more freeze after boot: a network freeze about 20–50 s after boot, caused by the time update, is fixed.
 
 **Mac tools**
-* TCI bridge for the Mac (tools/mac-serial-bridge): WS (formerly WSJT-X Improved), WSJT-X 3 and JTDX use the NAS-shared QMX as a TCI network radio, with receive audio (from the I/Q), CAT and transmit (FT8/FT4/JS8/WSPR tones) in one connection; no serial port or virtual audio device. The Tab5 keeps its own connection. Bench-tested against the relay's fake radio; not yet tested with WS on the air.
+* TCI bridge for the Mac (tools/mac-serial-bridge): WS (formerly WSJT-X Improved), WSJT-X 3 and JTDX use the NAS-shared QMX as a TCI network radio, with receive audio (from the I/Q), CAT and transmit (FT8/FT4/JS8/WSPR tones) in one connection; no serial port or virtual audio device. The Tab5 keeps its own connection; while a TCI program is connected the relay keeps the Tab5 off the transmitter (and the Mac off while the Tab5 transmits). Bench-tested against the relay's fake radio; not yet tested with WS on the air.
 * Build and flash from a Mac (tools/mac-build-flash.sh), and record the Tab5’s serial log (tools/mac-capture-serial.sh).
 
 **Keeping up with upstream**
